    "result": "The frai-core test suite is now fully passing! Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**1. Fixed governance test exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`):\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` constants\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n\n**2. Fixed evaluation metric parameter passing** (`src/eval/index.js`):\n   - Modified `runEvaluations` to check each metric function's arity (parameter count)\n   - Metrics expecting 1 parameter (just outputs) receive only outputs\n   - Metrics expecting 2 parameters receive outputs and references\n   - This prevents the `toxicityMetric` from receiving references as its banned terms parameter, which was causing it to incorrectly flag non-toxic content\n\n## Test Results\nAll 28 tests across 8 test files now pass:\n- \u2713 src/eval/index.test.js (3 tests)\n- \u2713 src/finetune/governance.test.js (5 tests)  \n- \u2713 src/questionnaire/run-questionnaire.test.js (4 tests)\n- \u2713 src/providers/openai.test.js (6 tests)\n- \u2713 src/documents/generate-documents.test.js (2 tests)\n- \u2713 src/config/key-store.test.js (2 tests)\n- \u2713 src/scanners/scan-codebase.test.js (2 tests)\n- \u2713 src/rag/index.test.js (4 tests)\n\nAll existing public exports remain working.",
